    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70-a1">

                <pb facs="0216" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg82"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 717.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Montufar to Mr.
                            Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 4,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: The United States of America have
                    given their support to Switzerland, which, although a Republic, is a European
                    nation, permitting the ministers and consuls of the American Union to lend their
                    good offices to the Swiss Cantons and to their citizens in those countries where
                    there are no ministers nor consuls of Switzerland.</p>
                <p>Guatemala, an American Republic, would see with pleasure the adoption of such a
                    measure in her favor. To-day I instruct our minister at Washington to make the
                    request of the American Government, and I ask you, if there is no objection, to
                    be pleased to write in the same sense so that the request may be well
                    received.</p>
                <p>This opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lorenzo
                            Montufar.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
